SLY Custom — ChangeLog
======================

Note: entries before 2.0.0 are a retroactive reconstruction from git history
(the module shipped with the version constant 1.0.0 throughout); 2.0.0 is the
first version managed through this file.

2.3.4 (2026-10-05)
- PDF templates: PHP 8 warning cleanup (production error-log noise,
  commande/error_log).
  pdf_sly_order.modules.php: add the missing $tab_height initialisation
  after the dynamic $tab_top computation — the template was forked from
  official eratosthene v14, which never initialised it either (official
  only added the line between v14 and v24). The note deduction and
  pdfTabTitles() now operate on a defined value; note that column
  separators of border-left columns, previously drawn zero-length
  (undefined -> null -> 0), now render as officially designed.
  pdf_sly_packinglist.modules.php + pdf_sly_shipment.modules.php: define
  the three posx layout properties (posxweightvol / posxqtyordered /
  posxqtytoship, values taken from official pdf_rouget) that were lost
  from the constructor when _tableau_tot / _pagehead were forked; values
  feed legacy layout math only (the Total row prints via
  printStdColumnContent), so no visual change.
- Patches: sly24.0-fourn-linkedobject.patch regenerated with the 7
  default_lang null-guards on fourn/facture/card.php (production
  "Attempt to read property default_lang on null" at setabsolutediscount
  PDF auto-regen; PHP 7 was silent). See APPLY-ON-24.md §6.5.
- Patches: sly24.0-langs.patch drops its fr_FR/main.lang segment (11 -> 10
  hunks) — both production and d-test pruned the fr_FR language pack, so
  the pre-prune segment could never apply ("No such file or directory").
  See APPLY-ON-24.md §6.6.
- fourn/facture/paiement.php: drop the vestigial RefSupplier header column.
  Upstream 24 removed the standalone column (body td commented, ref_supplier
  shown as subtitle in the Invoice cell); the SLY22 port kept the header th
  and the tfoot colspan counted it, so header/tfoot had one column more
  than every data row — the whole table and its Total row shifted by one
  column. Align on upstream 24 (th commented, colspan 5 -> 4, Type still
  +1). Patch regenerated (paiement.php section only). See APPLY-ON-24.md
  §6.7.

2.3.3 (2026-10-02)
- Hooks: PHP 8 warning cleanup for the ShipsGo delay computed extrafields
  (production error-log noise, compta/facture/error_log).
  Root cause: dol_eval() resolves a computed formula's $object to the PAGE
  global, not the object being fetched. When compta/facture/card.php creates
  an invoice from a shipment (fetch at card.php ~L3857 on the create form and
  ~L1816 on submit), core Expedition::fetch() -> fetch_optionals() evaluates
  the ATD/ATA delay formulas against the global $object — the Facture, whose
  array_options has no options_atd/options_ata keys — raising one
  "Undefined array key" warning per formula per request. Fix (module layer,
  no core patch): doActions() now also pre-defaults the four ShipsGo date
  keys on facture pages, so the formulas find the keys and short-circuit to
  ''. No functional change: the delay fields are shipment-display only and
  the invoice flow never consumed their values.
- Hooks: fixed the dead list-side guard in printFieldListValue() — it gated
  on the raw SQL row's $obj->element (never set on stdClass rows) and would
  have set keys on the row, while dol_eval() reads the PAGE $object; it now
  pre-defaults the keys on the list page's $object (element shipping/
  expedition). No-op today when MAIN_STORE_COMPUTED_EXTRAFIELDS is on (the
  list template then reads stored values and never evaluates); makes the
  guard actually effective if that constant is ever turned off.

2.3.2 (2026-10-02)
- PDF templates: PHP 8 warning cleanup (production error-log noise).
  pdf_sly_invoice.modules.php: removed the dead 2020 product-extrafield
  block (undefined $product/$rowid, sample field name
  options_my_product_extra, has written an empty cell for 5 years —
  fetch(null) was a no-op thanks to the core guard, so removal is
  behaviour-neutral); pdf_sly_invoice + pdf_cornas_SLY: initialise
  $outputlangsbis = null before the conditional creation so _tableau()
  calls stop raising "Undefined variable" when
  PDF_USE_ALSO_LANGUAGE_CODE is not set (aligns with the correct pattern
  already used in pdf_sly_order / pdf_sly_packinglist / pdf_sly_shipment).

2.2.18 (2026-09-28)
- patches: payment-table SUMMARY rows fixed (second round, same two files:
  sly24.0-compta-multicurrency.patch / compta/facture/card.php and
  sly24.0-fourn-linkedobject.patch / fourn/facture/card.php). 2.2.17 had
  fixed the header and payment rows to the v24 column order but left the
  bottom summary rows (Already paid / Billed / Remaining unpaid etc.) in
  the v22 layout: label cells used colspan=($nbcols+1) swallowing the MC
  column (MC amount rendered inside the narrow action cell), trailing
  <td>&nbsp;</td> created a phantom column, and a botched splice left an
  orphan <tr>-less fragment on the compta RemainderToPay row. Now all
  summary rows follow the unified v24-order pattern: label
  colspan=$nbcols + [MC amount td if column shown] + [action td: unlink
  icon for discounts, otherwise empty] + currency-formatted amount td.
  Credit-note RemainderToPayBack row rewritten the same way. Verified:
  17/17 patch replay on the authoritative git 24.0.1 baseline, replay
  trees byte-identical, php -l clean, and a static column-balance check
  across all 4 bank/MC scenarios = 0 mismatches on both cards.
- patches: SG date format PORT GAP closed — langs/en_SG/main.lang
  (FormatDateShort / FormatDateShortInput %d.%m.%Y -> %d/%m/%Y) was
  missing from the sly24 series: the v22 SLY tree customizes it but the
  patch build had missed it among ~550 unrelated lang-file additions in
  the dev worktree. Added to sly24.0-langs.patch as a MINIMAL port (only
  the two date lines; v24-native keys FormatHourSecShort / TotalVATShort
  are kept — a naive v22-file overlay would have deleted them).
- patches: AmountMulticurrency translation key — the payment table's MC
  column header ($langs->trans('AmountMulticurrency')) was SLY-introduced
  but never defined in any lang file (v22 hid the bug because the MC
  column rarely rendered; d-test2 with active multicurrency invoices
  shows the raw key). Defined in en_US/compta.lang and zh_CN/compta.lang
  (en_US fallback covers all en_* locales). One new line each, appended
  via minimum hunks. Replay 17/17 clean, 103 files / 0 CRLF.
- toolchain: pristine bundle sly24.0-pristine2401.tar.gz REBUILT after
  discovering the previous one (sha cce72aef…) was POISONED — its content
  was the sly24 ported working tree (101/101 files differ from git
  24.0.1), not pristine 24.0.1; the sha matching memory had merely
  proved it was the same poisoned file. New bundle: 103 entries (101
  original targets + langs/en_SG/main.lang for SG date format +
  langs/zh_CN/compta.lang), paths relative to htdocs, no directory
  entries, deterministic tar; every entry byte-compared against git tag
  24.0.1 (independent authority) and pure LF. New sha256:
  f3c58e8d62abba22d9d6df7cafda1e007c2c3c7d6e9a268fb7ae010786e4d9d2.
  BACKUP-GUIDE.md updated (old sha marked obsolete + poisoning lesson).
- OPS: on d-test2 — Restore the compta-multicurrency row then re-Apply
  with the updated patch; apply fourn-linkedobject as-is (still pending);
  apply the updated sly24.0-langs.patch for the SG date format (d-test2
  users must use the en_SG language to see it).
  If Restore/Reset was ever done with the OLD bundle on any environment,
  re-restore once with the new bundle to flush poisoned content.

2.2.17 (2026-09-23)
- patches: PAYMENT-TABLE structure bug fixed in TWO patch files (real
  port defects, the cause of the d-test2 "payment table 一直错位"):
  (a) sly24.0-compta-multicurrency.patch / compta/facture/card.php and
  (b) sly24.0-fourn-linkedobject.patch / fourn/facture/card.php.
  The v22 port had kept the v22 layout (amount last, action at end,
  header without an action column) while v24 moved the action column
  BEFORE Amount — and the port additionally emitted an orphan unclosed
  <td>, a duplicate amount cell per row, and (fourn) miscounted empty
  filler cells. Rows carried up to 3 more cells than the header.
  Fix: align to the v24 structure — header [AmountMulticurrency if shown]
  + Action (empty td restored) + Amount; rows [MC cell if] + single
  action td (delete) + single amount cell (currency-formatted).
  Sections regenerated from pristine 24.0.1 vs the corrected files and
  spliced into the patches; full 17-patch replay = 0 failures, php -l
  clean, replay byte-identical to the corrected sources, header/row cell
  counts balanced. Pristine bundle unaffected (it ships baseline files).
  OPS: on d-test2, Restore the compta-multicurrency row (per-patch
  backup exists) then re-Apply with the updated patch; fourn patch not
  yet applied — apply as-is when ready.

2.2.16 (2026-09-23)
- Shipment line totals migrated OFF computed extrafields onto the module
  layer, per the official v24 model (user directive: no core patches, no
  conf.php changes — official defaults only). Dolibarr 24's dol_eval
  whitelist ships no aggregation function, and the official extrafields
  help text (ComputedFormulaDesc3) confirms formulas are for scalar
  maths / object reloads, never line aggregation.
  (1) ActionsSlycustom::computeShipmentLineTotals() — shared static
      (qty / options_quantitycarton / options_grossweight sums).
  (2) Card display: doActions injects live totals into
      $object->array_options (options_totalnetweight / options_TotalQtyCartons /
      options_TotalGrossWeight) whenever lines are loaded — drafts included,
      stored values never zeroed in contexts without lines.
  (3) Persistence: SHIPMENT_VALIDATE trigger updates
      llx_expedition_extrafields so lists / exports / PDF substitution read
      stable stored values.
  Ops: the three extrafields must be converted from computed to PLAIN
  fields (clear the Computed formula box in Setup → Extra Fields →
  Shipment) — the formula would keep erroring under the official default
  whitelist. totalnetweight intentionally keeps the v22 formula's
  observable behaviour (sum of line qty); switch the source key in
  computeShipmentLineTotals() if true net weight is wanted.

2.2.15 (2026-09-23)
- REVERTED the 2.2.14 core hunk (expedition fetch_optionals ordering) after
  user review: "为什么要修改核心函数，而不是修改公式、遵守最新的规范？"
  Correct. Core-file changes are the last resort, not the first — and this
  one was added before the sanctioned config-level fix (the final
  $dolibarr_main_restrict_eval_methods line) had even been tested, and
  before establishing whether the already-applied core patch's display-time
  re-evaluation ($objectoffield = $this in showOptionals) already computes
  line-based formulas correctly once the whitelist passes them. Reverted:
  the other-modules hunk, the d24test source edit, target count back to
  101. The compliant fix path, in order: (1) conf.php whitelist line
  (norm-sanctioned — the error message itself names this parameter);
  (2) formulas stay as-is (date-diff ones optionally rewritten whitelist-
  free); (3) if the card still computes 0 after (1), the totals move to a
  slycustom HOOK (custom/ only, zero core changes, immune to dol_eval).
- Ops: sly24.0-pristine2401.tar.gz rebuilt with DETERMINISTIC tar flags
  (--sort=name --mtime fixed, gzip -n) so its sha256 is stable across
  rebuilds: cce72aef7c0f988d8514a0049df8ff1c9ca7f5024516d57e521ac248a90e18aa
  (101 entries). BACKUP-GUIDE §五 updated.

2.2.14 (2026-09-23)
- patches/sly24.0-other-modules.patch: NEW hunk for
  expedition/class/expedition.class.php — the first patch-content fix driven
  by the d-test2 diagnosis. Root cause of the "computed extrafields show 0"
  symptom: upstream v24 Expedition::fetch() calls fetch_optionals() (where
  computed extrafields are evaluated over $objectoffield->lines) BEFORE
  fetch_lines()/fetch_lines_free() — at evaluation time ->lines is empty, so
  SLY's line-aggregating formulas (total qty, total cartons, total gross
  weight via array_sum(array_column(...))) summed an empty array and always
  returned 0. v22 evaluated with the real object and worked. Fix: move the
  fetch_optionals() call to after the lines block (safe — fetch_lines*
  never reads the shipment's own array_options, grep-verified). Verified:
  pristine-24.0.1 replay of all 17 patches = 0 failures, php -l clean,
  replay byte-identical to the d24test source tree. Patch-series targets:
  101 → 102 files.
- Ops: sly24.0-pristine2401.tar.gz rebuilt with the 102nd target
  (sha256 63c3dda8d225c2157753a66816d14953124b0e82aacf641ea8f3ab8096410684);
  BACKUP-GUIDE §五 updated accordingly.
- Related (not patch-fixable, config/data level, documented in
  APPLY-ON-24.md §〇): Dolibarr 24 dol_eval() whitelist rejects isset etc.
  in migrated computed formulas — conf.php line required; line-aggregation
  formulas additionally need is_array/array_column/array_sum appended.

2.2.13 (2026-09-23)
- admin/patches.php: lintscan removed entirely (user directive: "补丁文件
  应该是你的责任，不是服务器应该做的" — patch QA belongs on the development
  side, never on the production server). Removed: the green "Diagnose:
  syntax scan" card, the lintscan action + its session resume keys, and the
  whole PHP-CLI discovery stack (slyPatchLintTargets, slyPatchFindPhpCli,
  slyPatchPhpCliValidates) — the exec-a-php-binary code surface that caused
  the 2.2.8-2.2.10 fpm flood no longer exists in the tool at all. Lang keys
  SlyPatchActionLintScan(+Hint)/SlyPatchLintPartial/SlyPatchLintPhpNone
  deleted (en_US, en_SG, zh_CN). The tool's server-side footprint is now
  git dry-runs, one git apply, and tar — nothing else. Patch verification
  (replay on pristine 24.0.1, php -l, function/class cross-checks, hunk
  review) happens in the dev repo before deployment.
- Patch-side note: full hunk-by-hunk runtime review of
  sly24.0-compta-multicurrency's compta/index.php changes found no fatal
  (SQL additions guarded by isModEnabled('multicurrency') with matching
  GROUP BY columns; price() called with the correct 7-parameter v24
  signature). The reproduced 500 remains undiagnosed pending the server
  error log (.user.ini error_log) — the only remaining diagnostic step.

2.2.12 (2026-09-23)
- admin/patches.php: slyPatchApply() reduced to the minimal model the tool
  should have had all along (user directive: "有原始备份文件，就不需要重新
  备份。直接patch"): backup target files that lack a pristine copy (never
  re-backup existing ones) → apply. Removed from the apply path: (1) the
  per-call session snapshot (a full second copy set of every target on
  EVERY apply, pure disk/IO load, read by nothing); (2) the automatic
  post-apply php -l syntax gate (one PHP process per target file per apply
  — the dominant process-spawn cost, and with 2.2.8-2.2.10's fpm-selection
  bug the very thing that flooded the host). Syntax diagnosis remains
  available on demand via the green lintscan card. Pack creation stays
  first-time-only from the pristine layer. Per single-patch Apply the tool
  now spawns exactly 3 processes: 2 git dry-runs (live apply decision) +
  1 git apply. Reset/Restore were already pure local `cp` from the
  per-patch pristine layer and are unchanged.

2.2.11 (2026-09-23)
- admin/patches.php: CRITICAL fix — PHP CLI discovery could select an FPM
  binary. The 2.2.8 validation only required `php -v` to start with "PHP "
  and exit 0, which `php-fpm -v` ("PHP 8.x (fpm-fcgi)...") also satisfies;
  the glob candidates (/usr/bin/php*, /usr/local/php*/bin/php, ...) can
  match fpm binaries. Once selected, every syntax-gate invocation ran
  `php-fpm -n -l <file>` — which does not lint anything but tries to START
  AN FPM MASTER DAEMON per call: the daemonized parent returns quickly so
  the "lint" reports success, while a persistent php process is left
  behind for every target file. On d-test2 this flooded the host with
  never-stopping processes (entry-process limit hit 40 times, server
  nearly unusable) and the poisoned path was cached to
  documents/slycustom/.phpcli so it kept happening on every later run.
  Fix: new slyPatchPhpCliValidates() requires the "(cli)" SAPI marker in
  the `php -v` first line; used both in the probe loop AND on every
  file-cache hit (one cheap exec per request), so a poisoned .phpcli cache
  file can never survive into a lint run again. RECOVERY for affected
  hosts: stop using the tool, kill the stray php processes (hosting panel
  PHP restart / support), delete documents/slycustom/.phpcli, deploy
  2.2.11, resume.

2.2.10 (2026-09-23)
- admin/patches.php: performance + correctness fix for shared-host
  throttling (d-test2: "each patch takes forever to apply, the server
  becomes nearly unavailable"). Root cause was process-spawn volume: every
  page view ran 2 git dry-runs per patch (34 spawns for 17 patches) in the
  status table, applyall re-ran the same 34 in its pre-scan, and every
  request re-probed PHP CLI candidates. On a host that throttles fork/exec
  each single-patch round trip spawned ~50 processes. Fixes:
  (1) slyPatchStatusCached() — session-cached status rows, 10-minute TTL;
      single-patch actions (applyone/restoreone) overwrite their own row
      with the deterministic outcome, applyall/smart-reset share one sweep,
      bulk actions (restore_bundle, restorefrompack, upload_bundle,
      resetone) drop the cache, and the Rescan button (?rescan=1) forces a
      fresh sweep; the view shows the snapshot age next to the Rescan
      button (SlyPatchStatusCacheNote).
  (2) slyPatchFindPhpCli() persists the discovered binary to
      documents/slycustom/.phpcli — one probe ever, not one per request
      (delete the file to re-probe).
  (3) slyPatchMakePack() now runs BEFORE the apply and tars the pristine
      per-patch BACKUP directory instead of DOL_DOCUMENT_ROOT — the old
      placement packed the PATCHED files, so every restore-from-pack was
      writing patched content back (the same poisoning class as the
      d-test2 bundle incident). Content is deterministic, so an existing
      pack for a patch is kept instead of re-tarring (saves 17 tar spawns
      per applyall). Packs already created by ≤2.2.9 hold patched content
      and should be deleted (packs/ dir) — the tool never reads them for
      pristine restores anymore, but keeping stale ones invites confusion.
- Langs en_US, en_SG, zh_CN: new key SlyPatchStatusCacheNote.

2.2.9 (2026-09-23)
- admin/patches.php: upload-bundle path turned into a true recovery primitive
  for the d-test2 incident ("first patch run OK, later modifications broke
  everything; now nothing applies and every patched page 500s"). Root-cause
  hypothesis, consistent with every symptom: the uploaded recovery bundle was
  packed from the sly24 PORT WORKTREE (already fully customized + later
  uncommitted edits), not from pristine 24.0.1. That single mistake (a) put
  already-patched content into htdocs, so every patch fails BOTH the forward
  and the reverse dry-run -> all Conflict, nothing can ever Apply again;
  (b) seeded the per-patch backup layer with that same non-pristine content,
  so every later Restore/Reset writes the poison back ("restore 之后仍然
  500"); (c) the worktree's later edits were never runtime-tested, explaining
  the 500s on exactly the pages with the most post-generation edits.
  Changes: (1) slyPatchIngestUploadedBundle now OVERWRITES existing per-patch
  backup files (an upload is an explicit reset-to-pristine operation asserted
  by the confirm dialog) and reports "Re-seeded (overwritten) N" in the log —
  the previous never-overwrite rule is exactly what kept poisoned backups
  undead. (2) The orange upload card now shows for ANY conflict state,
  including conflicts WITH backups (previously hidden when backups existed,
  i.e. precisely in the poisoned-backup scenario it must rescue). (3) Bundle
  layout tolerance: htdocs/<path> tar entries are accepted in addition to
  root-relative ones.
- Ops: guaranteed-pristine recovery bundle prebuilt locally from the git tag
  itself (`git archive 24.0.1` — no working tree involved):
  sly24.0-pristine2401.tar.gz (101 entries, ~1.4 MB,
  sha256 7dd28582c70aef59da38633b81272887dd6d0db665a51c618dad38b3631334d9).
  Upload it via the orange card, then Apply all — final state equals the
  locally 4-layer-verified replay (17/17 apply, 101/101 php -l clean).
- Langs en_US, en_SG, zh_CN: SlyPatchActionUploadBundleHint and
  SlyPatchUploadBundleConfirmText updated for the overwrite-reseed semantics.

2.2.8 (2026-09-22)
- admin/patches.php: lintscan hardened after it failed to complete on the
  d-test2 shared host. (1) PHP CLI discovery now probes candidate binaries —
  command -v php, PHP_BINARY (excluding fpm/cgi/httpd), /usr/bin/php*,
  /usr/local/bin/php*, cPanel /opt/cpanel/ea-php*/root/usr/bin/php and Plesk
  layouts — validating each with `php -v` and reporting the tried list when
  none works. (2) The scan is time-boxed (20s per request, set_time_limit(0)
  requested) and chunked: when the budget elapses it stores its position and
  the accumulated bad-file list in the session and asks for one more click
  (SlyPatchLintPartial), instead of dying mid-scan on 30-60s hosting request
  timeouts. Verified locally: all 17 patches replay cleanly on a pristine
  24.0.1 tree (git apply -p2 --ignore-whitespace, 0 failures) and all 101
  target files pass php -l — the series itself is syntax-clean.
- Langs en_US, en_SG, zh_CN: new keys SlyPatchLintPartial, SlyPatchLintPhpNone.

2.2.7 (2026-09-22)
- admin/patches.php: post-apply syntax gate in slyPatchApply(). After the
  engine reports success, every .php target of the patch is passed through
  `php -l` (CLI binary discovered once via command -v; lint is skipped
  with a log line when no CLI is on PATH). Any syntax error — the signature
  of a patch applied onto a drifted baseline (different 24.0.x) or of a
  truncated write — fails the apply AND restores every target from the
  pristine per-patch backup captured moments earlier, so a broken file can
  never stay in the tree. Motivated by the d-test2 compta/index.php 500
  after the first successful applyall (2026-09-22): the patch series was
  verified against pristine 24.0.1, so a live 500 means the server tree
  differs from that baseline — this gate turns such a mismatch into a
  clean refuse+rollback instead of a production 500. Log lines carry the
  full php -l output per broken file.
- admin/patches.php: shell-free diagnostics for the d-test2 shared-host
  deployment (no SSH): new action=lintscan + green card "Diagnose: syntax
  scan (php -l)" runs slyPatchLintTargets() over the union of all patch
  targets (read-only) and reports in the persisted on-page log. The page
  intro now always shows the live DOL_VERSION and flags non-24.0.1 trees
  ("patches are generated against the 24.0.1 baseline") — a drifted 24.0.x
  baseline is the leading suspect for post-apply 500s.
- Langs en_US, en_SG, zh_CN: new keys SlyPatchActionLintScan(+Hint).

2.2.6 (2026-09-22)
- admin/patches.php: fixed the path-prefix mismatch surfaced by the new
  conflict diagnostic box on d-test2 ("error: htdocs/core/... No such file
  or directory"): the sly24.0-*.patch headers are REPO-ROOT relative
  ("+++ b/htdocs/<path>", produced by gen_sly24_patches.sh which diffs
  from the repository root), but the engine ran `cd DOL_DOCUMENT_ROOT`
  (= htdocs) with -p1, resolving every target to <htdocs>/htdocs/<path>.
  Consequences went beyond the apply failure: slyPatchTargetFiles()
  returned htdocs/-prefixed paths, so backups / packs / bundles /
  upload-whitelist all pointed at non-existent nested paths — a "Create
  bundle" on a clean tree reported success while packing NOTHING
  ("every unioned target is a new file"). Fixes:
  * slyPatchEngine(): -p1 -> -p2 for both engines (strips "a/htdocs/"),
    cd DOL_DOCUMENT_ROOT unchanged.
  * slyPatchTargetFiles(): strips a leading "htdocs/" segment when
    present, so every consumer (backup paths, packs, bundle, target
    list, upload whitelist, file-to-patches map) now works in
    DOL_DOCUMENT_ROOT-relative paths. Verified: 101 targets across the
    17 patches, zero still-prefixed, 101/101 resolve to real files on
    the local tree.
- patches/BACKUP-GUIDE.md: troubleshooting table gains the prefix-
  mismatch row; space-budget section's per-patch file counts were early
  estimates — the real union is 101 files.

2.2.5 (2026-09-22)
- admin/patches.php + patches/: three stacked root causes behind the
  d-test2 "every patch conflict on a never-patched pristine 24.0.1" report,
  all identified and fixed:
  1. CRLF patch files (primary): all 17 sly24.0-*.patch files carried
     Windows CRLF line endings (the dev machine has core.autocrlf=true, so
     the git checkout materialised them as CRLF; deploying by file copy
     shipped those bytes to Linux). `git apply` treats the trailing CR as
     part of the `+++ b/<file>` header and of every context line, so BOTH
     the forward and the reverse dry-runs fail and a perfectly clean tree
     reports "conflict" for all 17 patches. Fixes:
     * All patch files converted to LF in the repo; new
       patches/.gitattributes (*.patch text eol=lf) prevents autocrlf from
       re-introducing CRLF on Windows checkouts.
     * Runtime defence: slyPatchNormalizePatchFile() — slyPatchStatus()
       and slyPatchApply() feed the engine an LF-normalised copy
       (.norm_<name> staged under patch-backups/) whenever the stored
       patch contains a CR, so the tool is immune regardless of how the
       files reach the server.
  2. dol_mkdir() return-value bug: dol_mkdir() returns 0 for "already
     exists" (<0 KO, >0 created), but MakePack / MakeBundle /
     IngestUploadedBundle tested it as boolean (`!dol_mkdir(...)`) — every
     pack/bundle build after the first one failed with a bogus "could not
     create dir .../packs" (d-test2: first Create-bundle OK, every later
     one "failed"). New truth-proof slyPatchEnsureDir() (is_dir before and
     after) replaces those three checks.
  3. git dubious-ownership hardening: when htdocs is a git checkout owned
     by a different user than php-fpm (typical for /home/<user> hosting),
     git >= 2.35.2 fatals with "detected dubious ownership", failing every
     status check the same way. The git engine templates now carry
     `-c safe.directory=<DOL_DOCUMENT_ROOT>` (older git ignores the key).
- New conflict diagnostic box above the patch table: when a patch reports
  conflict and the engine produced output, the raw git/patch stderr (first
  25 lines) is shown directly on the page instead of only in the badge
  hover tooltip — CRLF and ownership failures would have been visible
  immediately instead of taking two debugging rounds.
- Table rows are buffered (ob_start per row) so the diagnostic box can be
  printed before the table; row content unchanged.
- Langs en_US, en_SG, zh_CN: new key SlyPatchConflictDiagIntro.
- patches/BACKUP-GUIDE.md: new troubleshooting section 七 (all-conflict
  checklist: CRLF / safe.directory / diagnose via the new box).

2.2.4 (2026-09-22)
- admin/patches.php: full logic + design audit on top of the upload-bundle
  recovery path; findings and fixes:
  * FATAL (own bug, pre-emptied): $conflictPatchesList /
    $missingPerPatchList were not initialised before the status loop — on a
    "conflict but backup exists" tree the card code hit count(null) and
    PHP 8 TypeError-fatals the page. Both now initialised to array().
  * Lost logs: every POST redirects before rendering, so the detailed
    engine log (per-patch results, backup paths, failure output) never
    reached the browser and the on-page log box was dead code. The action
    handler now persists $logs into $_SESSION['slypatch_lastlogs']; the
    view shows it once after the redirect and clears it.
  * upload_bundle size cap 32MB -> 16MB: a cap at the post_max_size limit
    gets rejected by PHP at the protocol layer with $_FILES empty,
    surfacing as a misleading "no file in upload field". Basename regex
    simplified to the same pattern as restorefrompack.
  * Lang placeholders %d -> %s (SlyPatchNoBackupNotice,
    SlyPatchUploadBundleOk): Dolibarr trans() only reliably substitutes
    %s.
  * upload_bundle now raises setEventMessages on success (restored +
    seeded counts via SlyPatchUploadBundleOk) and on failure
    (SlyPatchUploadBundleFailed), alongside the persisted detailed log.
  * Security model unified across all three tar.gz consumers
    (upload ingest / restorefrompack / restore_bundle): verbose
    tar -tvzf listing parsed to refuse symlink / hardlink / device
    entries BEFORE extraction, traversal check, and a hard whitelist —
    slyPatchRestoreFromPack previously extracted any relative path
    (packs can be planted cross-host), it now refuses entries outside
    the union of all patch target files.
  * slyPatchRestoreFilesFromBackup returns a structured 'missing' flag;
    the resetapplyall_smart / resetone handlers stop sniffing the
    English log-string prefix.
  * slyPatchIngestUploadedBundle: single source of truth for the
    whitelist (keys of slyPatchFileToPatchesMap — no second, drift-prone
    whitelist), ?? guard on the per-file patch list, log line with
    coverage (N/M target files present in the archive), duplicated
    recursive staging-dir cleanup extracted into slyPatchRmDirTree().
  * Dead code removed: unused global $db / global $PATCHES; legacy lang
    keys SlyPatchResetOneFallbackConfirmText and SlyPatchResetSmartHint
    (superseded by SlyPatchActionResetConflictHint) in all three langs.
- admin/patches.php: recovery path for the deadlock reported on d-test where
  every sly24.0-*.patch reports Conflict AND the per-patch backup layer is
  missing (applied by an older slycustom release that lacked this layer, or
  backups were wiped) — the local-only model of 2.2.3 left such an
  environment with no way out. New operator-driven upload path, still zero
  network / zero git:
  * New helpers: slyPatchExtractTarGz (tar -tzf pre-flight refusing '..' /
    absolute paths, then tar -xzf into a temp dir), slyPatchFileToPatchesMap
    (reverse map: htdocs-relative path -> patch short names touching it),
    slyPatchIngestUploadedBundle (extracts the uploaded tar.gz, copies each
    whitelisted target file into DOL_DOCUMENT_ROOT AND seeds
    patch-backups/per-patch/<name>/ for every patch touching it — honouring
    the never-overwrite rule), slyPatchDownloadTargetList (streams the union
    of all patch target paths as a plain text list).
  * New GET action downloadtargetlist (token-gated, mirrors downloadpack):
    downloads sly24.0-target-list.txt for offline bundle building.
  * New POST action upload_bundle: whitelists the uploaded basename against
    ^sly24\.0-(bundle|[a-zA-Z0-9_.-]+)_[A-Za-z0-9_.-]*\.tar\.gz$, caps the
    size at 32MB, rejects any PHP upload error, then runs the ingest. Every
    archive entry outside the patch-target whitelist is silently dropped.
  * Workflow (documented in BACKUP-GUIDE.md §五): download the target list,
    tar the same paths on a pristine 24.0.1 clone, upload the tar.gz; the
    tool restores htdocs to the clean baseline and seeds per-patch backups
    so future Resets are a pure local cp again.
- admin/patches.php UI: bottom action bar rebuilt as severity-coded cards
  (green left band = safe [apply all / create bundle], red = destructive
  [restore from bundle / reset conflicting + apply all], orange = warning
  [the new upload-bundle recovery card]). Replaces the previous "two red
  boxes + bare inline forms" layout. Each card: title + one-line plain
  hint + buttons on the right. The reset card shows a live count of
  conflict patches missing their per-patch backup when > 0.
  New CSS classes .slypatch-actions / .slypatch-action / .safe / .warn /
  .danger scoped to this page only.
- Status scan loop now also collects conflictPatchesList +
  missingPerPatchList (conflict patches whose per-patch backup dir is
  absent) to drive the new cards' visibility.
- Langs en_US, en_SG, zh_CN: new keys SlyPatchActionApplyAll(+Hint),
  SlyPatchActionCreateBundle(+Hint), SlyPatchActionRestoreBundle(+Hint),
  SlyPatchActionResetConflict(+Hint), SlyPatchActionUploadBundle(+Hint),
  SlyPatchDownloadTargetList, SlyPatchUploadBundleConfirmText,
  SlyPatchNoBackupNotice, SlyPatchUploadBundleOk,
  SlyPatchUploadBundleFailed.
- patches/BACKUP-GUIDE.md: new §五 "当逐项备份缺失时——上传 Bundle 兜底"
  (scenario, offline build steps, security boundaries); §五→§六 renumbered
  (space budget).

2.2.3 (2026-09-22)
- admin/patches.php: dropped every external rollback source. Per user
  directive, the only rollback sources for sly24.0-*.patch are now the
  local pre-bundled backups (per-file per-patch backup + per-patch
  pack tar.gz + cross-patch bundle tar.gz) — no git checkout, no
  github archive download, no archive upload. The first applyall on
  a clean Dolibarr 24.0.1 tree is the one-time setup that populates
  the per-patch backups; from then on every Reset / Restore is a
  pure local `cp` away.
  * Removed helpers (200+ LOC, no longer referenced):
    - slyPatchDetect24Base() — local git tag 24.0.1 probe.
    - slyPatchDownloadOfficialTarball() — github tarball download
      with dolibarr.org fallback (90MB cache at
      documents/slycustom/downloads/).
    - slyPatchResetCore2401() — bulk `git checkout 24.0.1 -- htdocs/`.
    - slyPatchResetFilesFrom2401() — per-file `git checkout 24.0.1`.
    - slyPatchResetFilesFromExtractedRoot() — per-file copy from
      extracted 24.0.1 archive.
    - slyPatchExtractArchive() / slyPatchArchiveExt() /
      slyPatchExtractedStaysInRoot() — tar/zip extract path.
    - slyPatchRrmDir() / slyPatchRecursivelyCopy() — used only by
      the deleted reset helpers.
  * resetapplyall_smart: now uses each conflict patch's own
    per-patch backup (documents/slycustom/patch-backups/per-patch/
    <name>/) as the only restore source. Bulk-conflict file inventory
    is gone — we just restore the conflict patches in sequence. If any
    conflict patch has no per-patch backup, the bulk action refuses
    with a precise list of missing patches + three recovery paths
    (lang key SlyPatchResetLocalFailed). Other htdocs files stay
    untouched, so this remains safe to run on a partially-customised
    deployment.
  * resetone: dropped the git / auto-download fallback. Per-patch
    backup is the only source. If the backup is missing, Reset
    refuses with the same SlyPatchResetLocalFailed message naming the
    specific patch.
  * Top docblock: rewritten to reflect the local-only rollback model.
  * UI: bulk-button confirm text now flows through
    SlyPatchResetConflictConfirmText (replaces the hardcoded English
    prompt). Per-row Reset no longer needs the fallback-confirm
    branch (it never falls back anywhere).
  * Langs: en_US, en_SG, zh_CN. SlyPatchResetSmartHint and
    SlyPatchResetAllFailed rewritten to drop the git / download
    language. New key SlyPatchResetLocalFailed with the three
    recovery paths. SlyPatchResetConflictConfirmText added.
    SlyPatchResetOneFallbackConfirmText retained as a legacy marker
    (no longer referenced by code).
  * patches/BACKUP-GUIDE.md: section 1 table now lists only the
    three local-snapshot layers + per-patch pack + bundle (rows 3
    and 4 — the git/download layers — removed). Section 4.6 updated
    to recommend Bundle Restore as the "violent rollback" path; the
    old slyPatchResetCore2401 path is mentioned as a removed
    feature. A new first row in the table highlights "fresh git
    clone + install/upgrade" as the one-time manual setup.

2.2.2 (2026-09-21)
- New "pack layer" backup mechanism on top of the existing per-file
  per-patch backup in admin/patches.php: every successful slyPatchApply
  call now also writes one tar.gz holding every pristine (pre-patch) file
  that patch would touch, under
  documents/slycustom/patch-backups/packs/sly24.0-<name>_<ts>.tar.gz.
  Per-file backup stays as the source of truth for offline rollback; the
  pack is a single portable artifact that complements it (download /
  upload / cross-env rollback).
  * slyPatchMakePack(): builds a list of patch targets (only files that
    exist on disk; new files are skipped) and runs `tar -czf ... -T list`
    with a random-suffix dotfile manifest cleaned up afterwards.
    Failures are reported in the apply log but do NOT fail the apply.
  * slyPatchListPacks($name): scans packs/ for sly24.0-<name>_*.tar.gz,
    returns mtime-sorted descending. Drives the row UI and the top banner.
  * slyPatchRestoreFromPack($pack): whitelists the basename with a strict
    regex (sly24.0-[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+.tar.gz), basenames any caller input,
    runs `tar -tzf` to enumerate entries, refuses path-traversal ('..'
    segments / absolute paths) before any extraction, then `tar -xzf`
    from DOL_DOCUMENT_ROOT. Used by the new per-row "Restore from pack"
    button and the new bulk action=restorefrompack GET handler.
  * Top-of-page info banner: live count + KB total across all packs in
    packs/ (lang key SlyPatchPacksSummary).
  * Per-row UI: "Download pack" link (GET, token-gated, headers
    Content-Disposition: attachment) streams the latest pack for that row.
    "Restore from pack" button (POST, CSRF + whitelist) is shown for
    status in {applied, conflict} when at least one pack exists.
  * Langs: en_US, en_SG, zh_CN.
- New "bundle" backup layer on top of the per-patch pack layer for the
  cross-patch overlap case: when two or more sly24.0-*.patch files touch
  the same htdocs-relative path (e.g. core + remx + other-modules all
  edit htdocs/main.inc.php), each per-patch pack captures the post-prior
  state, so a single per-patch restore yields the wrong intermediate
  value. The bundle is one tar.gz holding the deduped UNION of every
  patch target, captured at the start of every applyall BEFORE the chain
  begins — gives a single consistent "pre-applyall" snapshot.
  * slyPatchAllTargetFiles(): reads every patch's `+++ b/...` headers,
    dedupes into a single sorted list. Drives the bundle build.
  * slyPatchMakeBundle(): writes sly24.0-bundle_<ts>.tar.gz to packs/.
    Auto-invoked at the start of every applyall; failures are logged but
    do NOT block the chain. Old bundles are never auto-deleted.
  * slyPatchLatestBundle(): returns (basename, mtime) of the latest
    bundle on disk. Drives the "Restore from bundle" button.
  * New actions: bundle_create (manual snapshot, no apply) and
    restore_bundle (one-tar.gz rollback via existing
    slyPatchRestoreFromPack whose basename whitelist already accepts the
    sly24.0-bundle_*.tar.gz naming).
  * UI: top-of-page info banner now lists both "N pack(s) tar.gz, X KB"
    AND "Latest bundle: <name> (<ts>)". Two new bottom buttons:
    "Create bundle" and a red alert-style "Restore from bundle" (only
    visible when a bundle exists on disk).
  * Langs: en_US, en_SG, zh_CN. New keys: SlyPatchBundleLatest,
    SlyPatchBundleNone, SlyPatchCreateBundle, SlyPatchRestoreBundle,
    SlyPatchCreateBundleConfirmText, SlyPatchRestoreBundleConfirmText.

2.2.1 (2026-09-21)
- New admin tool admin/patches.php (entry button on the setup General tab):
  browser-based application of the sly24.0-*.patch core series. Live status
  per patch via reverse dry-run (applied / not applied / conflict), one-click
  "apply all" in dependency order, automatic backup of every touched file to
  documents/slycustom/patch-backups/<timestamp>/, admin-only + CSRF + patch
  name whitelist + DOL_VERSION 24.x guard. Engine: git apply with fallback
  to POSIX patch. Langs: en_SG, en_US, zh_CN.
- Bugfix: patch engine command used `-p2` but the sly24.0-*.patch headers only
  carry one prefix segment (`a/htdocs/...`); switched to `-p1`.
- Bugfix: 5 lang keys referenced by sly24.0-remx.patch (SplitDiscountOptions
  AndAmounts, RemxSplitLocalCurrency, RemxSplitOriginalCurrency, SplitInto,
  LastPartCalculatedAutomatically) were missing from the official Dolibarr
  24.0.1 lang files; added to en_SG / en_US / zh_CN.
- Bugfix: sly24.0-commande.patch hunk at htdocs/commande/card.php @@ -40,23
  +40,9@@ wrongly 3way-deleted `require_once '/core/class/html.formfile
  .class.php'` while leaving `new FormFile($db)` at line 2142 — produced a
  "Class FormFile not found" fatal when commande/card.php was loaded. hunk
  rewritten as `-40,23 +40,24@@` to keep all upstream require_once and only
  add `files.lib.php`.
- New action `resetapplyall_smart` for the case where d-test htdocs/ is in a
  partial-applied state (admin/patches.php badge shows "Conflict" for one or
  more patches): the smart reset is **per-file surgical** — it scans every
  patch for status=Conflict, unions the `+++ b/...` target-file lists into
  a single set, then restores only those N files to their official 24.0.1
  contents. Every other file in DOL_DOCUMENT_ROOT (customisations, hooks,
  files not touched by any core patch, ad-hoc user edits) stays exactly
  where it was. Source priority (one click tries them in order, no user
  input required):
    1. local git tag `24.0.1` (`git checkout 24.0.1 -- <path>` per file)
    2. auto-download the official 24.0.1 tarball from
       https://github.com/Dolibarr/dolibarr/archive/refs/tags/24.0.1.tar.gz
       (cached at documents/slycustom/downloads/, falls back to the dolibarr
       .org stable URL)
  Pre-reset copies of every touched file are saved to
  documents/slycustom/patch-backups/file-reset-<ts>/<path> so recovery is
  one directory away. After the surgical reset the page chains into the
  normal 17-patch apply-all so the freshly re-baselined tree ends with all
  SLY customisations reapplied. Removed: the user-uploaded archive branch —
  d-test post_max_size=32M, the 24.0.1 tarball is 90MB, so any upload attempt
  fails at the PHP protocol layer (POST Content-Length exceeds limit) and
  breaks the whole form. The remaining two sources are sufficient: per-patch
  backup (handled by per-row Reset, local cp), then git tag / auto-download
  (handled by this bulk action). Removed the now-unused slyPatchReplaceHtdocs
  helper (was the old "replace entire htdocs/" path).
- New per-row Apply / Reset / Restore buttons in the patches table: every
  successful `slyPatchApply` call now also writes a stable per-patch backup
  to documents/slycustom/patch-backups/per-patch/<name>/<rel> (honours
  whatever is already on disk — never overwrites with a partially-patched
  copy), so the per-row Reset is a local `cp -r` away: no network, no git,
  no archive extraction. The bulk `resetapplyall_smart` button stays as
  the one-click recovery for first-run / wiped-backup scenarios.
    * Apply   (status=not applied) — clean forward apply, only this patch.
    * Reset   (status=conflict)    — copy the per-patch backup back and
      re-apply so the row lands on "applied"; if the per-patch backup is
      missing, falls back through the same git 24.0.1 → auto-download
      chain that `resetapplyall_smart` uses.
    * Restore (status=applied)    — copy the per-patch backup back and
      stop; row becomes "not applied".
  All three new actions validate the patch name against the whitelist,
  refuse any path that smells like `..`, and run inside the same CSRF +
  admin-only + DOL_VERSION 24.x guard as the existing apply-all.
- ShipsGo date-extrafield keys (options_atd / options_etd / options_ata /
  options_eta): ensured present on $object->array_options before any
  dol_eval() runs, via the new ensureShipmentDateOptionKeys() helper in
  custom/slycustom/class/actions_slycustom.class.php. Called from both
  doActions() (expedition card, view + edit) and printFieldListValue()
  (expedition list rows). Pure module-layer hook, no core patch. Eliminates
  the PHP 8.1+ "Undefined array key options_atd / options_ata" Warning that
  the extrafield computed-formula itself cannot suppress (formula cannot
  use isset / ?? / empty).
- Housekeeping: sly22.0-*.patch (17 patches + 2 SQL) and APPLY-ON-22.md /
  gen_sly22_patches.sh moved into patches/archive/ to keep the patches/
  root directory focused on the active sly24.0 series. README.md and
  PATCHES-BY-MODULE.md updated with a "historical document, archive/"
  notice; modSlyCustom.class.php + ActionsSlycustomMenuHooksTrait.php
  comments and the module README reference the 24-series patch names.

